Notebook[{
Cell["FindAdvancingInfraFront", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"410c5f3e-59e2-41c0-98d5-87573e08ed51"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"d3d39f3e-b563-4ce4-92d8-622b4e85ad9b"],

Cell["\<\
FindAdvancingInfraFront[graph, origin, steps] returns the foliation { \
InfraSet[S_0], ..., InfraSet[S_steps] } of a bouncing wavefront from origin. \
Each step moves every front vertex u one geodesic step outward from the \
previous front S_{i-1} (to the neighbours v with d(S_{i-1},v) == \
d(S_{i-1},u)+1), and reflects it back inward where there is no outward \
neighbour, so the front expands as a thin metric shell and turns straight \
around at a boundary or focus -- it never empties and never dwells, unlike \
the metric-sphere shell FindInfraShell which dies at the eccentricity. The \
state is the pair (S_{i-1}, S_i), so the rule is a NestList on \
consecutive-front pairs (the discrete second-order/wave form, momentum \
carried as the trailing front). origin is a single vertex (bare label, \
including a list-vertex {i,j}) or an InfraPoint[{v1,...,vk}] multi-source \
seed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69a5309b-031a-4be8-b918-54e5d1473453"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b85ba453-bc94-4de7-ab08-8cfc8e7a2be3"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"e9f213db-2514-4b03-90ee-9f1434ae08bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"9a23b1b2-00e2-46bb-976e-467adac3fe97"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"85bb143c-72cd-4fa6-9ac8-bb3d6b685d60"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dff043b7-8f77-4cbd-afd5-668e4e639fce"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d22dd72a-b4ca-4aad-9f76-50f2627f3e84"]
},
